{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_012","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"Copy page as Markdown for LLMs","location_hint":"paragraph 73","char_start":1634,"char_end":1664,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_013","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"Permission delegation defines permissions that can be granted to other accounts. These permissions fall into the following categories:","location_hint":"paragraph 84","char_start":1922,"char_end":2056,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_014","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"Transaction Type Permissions - Permission to send transactions with the specified transaction type .","location_hint":"paragraph 85","char_start":2060,"char_end":2160,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_015","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"Granular Permissions - Permission to send transactions with a specific subset of functionality.","location_hint":"paragraph 86","char_start":2162,"char_end":2257,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_016","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"Requires the PermissionDelegation amendment . Loading...","location_hint":"paragraph 87","char_start":2261,"char_end":2317,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_017","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"In the canonical binary format for transactions and ledger data, permission values are stored in a numeric form (specifically, as a 32-bit unsigned integer). However, in JSON they can be specified and returned in string format for convenience, similar to how transaction type names ( TransactionType fields) work.","location_hint":"paragraph 89","char_start":2346,"char_end":2659,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_018","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"When specifying a permission value in JSON, you can use either the numeric value or the string value. When serving data, the server supplies the string value if it is known, and falls back to the numeric value otherwise.","location_hint":"paragraph 90","char_start":2661,"char_end":2881,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_019","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"Not all client libraries support numeric PermissionValue types. In most cases, you should use the string names of the permissions you want to grant.","location_hint":"paragraph 92","char_start":2894,"char_end":3042,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_020","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"For transaction type permissions , the string is the name of the transaction type exactly (case-sensitive). For example, a permission value of \"PaymentChannelClaim\" grants permission to send PaymentChannelClaim transactions .","location_hint":"paragraph 93","char_start":3046,"char_end":3271,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_021","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"For granular permissions , the string is the name of the granular permission (case-sensitive). For example, a permission value of \"TrustlineAuthorize\" grants permission to send TrustSet transactions that authorize trust lines (but not ones that modify other settings such as the trust line limit or freeze status).","location_hint":"paragraph 94","char_start":3273,"char_end":3587,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_022","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"The numeric value 0 is reserved for \"full permissions\", meaning permission to send transactions of all types, but it is not possible to delegate full permissions.","location_hint":"paragraph 95","char_start":3591,"char_end":3753,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_023","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"Transaction Type Permissions have numeric values from 1 to 65536 (that is, 2 16 ), inclusive. They correspond with known transaction types, except you add 1 when specifying a transaction type as a permission value. For example, the string \"Payment\" corresponds to a TransactionType value of 0 , but a PermissionValue value of 1 . To grant permissions to make Payment transactions, you can specify either \"PermissionValue\": \"Payment\" or \"PermissionValue\": 1 .","location_hint":"paragraph 97","char_start":3785,"char_end":4243,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_024","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"For a mapping of transaction types known by a server and their corresponding numeric transaction type values, check the TRANSACTION_TYPES field in the server_definitions method .","location_hint":"paragraph 98","char_start":4245,"char_end":4423,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_025","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"List of Non-Delegatable Permissions","location_hint":"paragraph 99","char_start":4425,"char_end":4460,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_026","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"Some transaction types can&#x27;t be delegated. If you attempt to grant these permissions to a delegate, the transaction fails with a result code such as tecNO_PERMISSION . This includes all transaction types that can be used to grant other permissions to different key pairs or accounts. Additionally, all pseudo-transaction types can&#x27;t be delegated since they can&#x27;t be sent by normal accounts anyway.","location_hint":"paragraph 100","char_start":4462,"char_end":4874,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_027","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"The following permissions cannot be delegated:","location_hint":"paragraph 101","char_start":4876,"char_end":4922,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_028","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"Transaction Type Permission Value","location_hint":"paragraph 102","char_start":4926,"char_end":4959,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_029","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"With only the PermissionDelegation amendment, it&#x27;s possible to assign permissions for transaction types that are reserved, unassigned, or part of amendments that are not currently enabled; it&#x27;s also possible to assign PermissionValue 0 for full permissions. However, these values do not actually grant any permissions. This is a bug, and a future amendment will prevent assigning values outside of currently-enabled, delegatable transaction types or known granular permissions.","location_hint":"paragraph 113","char_start":5130,"char_end":5617,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_030","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"Granular Permissions have numeric types of 65537 and up, corresponding to specific names of permissions. Values that are not defined are not allowed. Each granular permission is a subset of a single transaction type&#x27;s functionality.","location_hint":"paragraph 116","char_start":5651,"char_end":5888,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_031","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"Numeric Value Name Transaction Type Description","location_hint":"paragraph 117","char_start":5892,"char_end":5939,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_032","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"65537 TrustlineAuthorize TrustSet Can authorize individual trust lines .","location_hint":"paragraph 118","char_start":5943,"char_end":6015,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_033","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"65538 TrustlineFreeze TrustSet Can freeze individual trust lines .","location_hint":"paragraph 119","char_start":6017,"char_end":6083,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_034","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"65539 TrustlineUnfreeze TrustSet Can unfreeze individual trust lines .","location_hint":"paragraph 120","char_start":6085,"char_end":6155,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_035","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"65540 AccountDomainSet AccountSet Can set the Domain field of the account.","location_hint":"paragraph 121","char_start":6157,"char_end":6231,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_036","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"65541 AccountEmailHashSet AccountSet Can set the EmailHash field of the account.","location_hint":"paragraph 122","char_start":6233,"char_end":6313,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_037","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"65542 AccountMessageKeySet AccountSet Can set the MessageKey field of the account.","location_hint":"paragraph 123","char_start":6315,"char_end":6397,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_038","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"65543 AccountTransferRateSet AccountSet Can set the transfer fee of fungible tokens issued by the account .","location_hint":"paragraph 124","char_start":6399,"char_end":6506,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_039","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"65544 AccountTickSizeSet AccountSet Can set the tick size of fungible tokens issued by the account .","location_hint":"paragraph 125","char_start":6508,"char_end":6608,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_040","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"65545 PaymentMint Payment Can send payments that mint new fungible tokens or MPTs.","location_hint":"paragraph 126","char_start":6610,"char_end":6692,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_041","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"65546 PaymentBurn Payment Can send payments that burn fungible tokens or MPTs.","location_hint":"paragraph 127","char_start":6694,"char_end":6772,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_042","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"65547 MPTokenIssuanceLock MPTokenIssuanceSet Can lock the balances of a particular MPT issued by the account.","location_hint":"paragraph 128","char_start":6774,"char_end":6883,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_043","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"Requires the MPTokensV1 amendment . Loading...","location_hint":"paragraph 129","char_start":6885,"char_end":6931,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_044","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"65548 MPTokenIssuanceUnlock MPTokenIssuanceSet Can unlock the balances of a particular MPT issued by the account.","location_hint":"paragraph 130","char_start":6935,"char_end":7048,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_045","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"Requires the MPTokensV1 amendment . Loading...","location_hint":"paragraph 131","char_start":7050,"char_end":7096,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_046","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"Limitations to Granular Permissions","location_hint":"paragraph 132","char_start":7102,"char_end":7137,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_047","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"The set of granular permissions is hard-coded. No custom configurations are allowed. For example, you cannot add permissions based on specific currencies. Adding a new granular permission requires an amendment.","location_hint":"paragraph 133","char_start":7139,"char_end":7349,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_206907715043_048","source_id":"src_206907715043","source_hash":"7d291105ddd546f52ed92efc652468f3492a5c9f1ad9f0c5a65a6c196c7ab6d7","text":"Numeric and String Values Transaction Type Permissions List of Non-Delegatable Permissions Granular Permissions Limitations to Granular Permissions","location_hint":"paragraph 141","char_start":7502,"char_end":7649,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:58:50.615Z"}
